{"type":"message","id":"34e12ee3","parentId":"e9519e04","timestamp":"2026-05-19T01:17:56.337Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, the PKCS1 and PKCS8 keys look the same! That's because the new key was generated directly and pkcs8 conversion just wraps it. The issue is that the Python SDK's `load_private_key` function is trying to load it as both DER formats first, then PEM. But the key format detection is confused because both PKCS1 and PKCS8 PEM formats start differently.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the error: `MismatchedTags(\"RSA PRIVATE KEY\", \"PRIVATE KEY\")`. The SDK expects `-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----` (PKCS#1) format but the key has `-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----` (PKCS#8).\n\n\nI need to generate a PKCS#1 format key with the correct header to satisfy what the SDK is expecting.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_aa85107fda57440587de5844","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Generate PKCS#1 format key (RSA PRIVATE KEY header)\nopenssl genrsa -out /tmp/tiger_rsa_pkcs1.pem 2048 2>&1\n\necho \"=== RSA PRIVATE KEY (PKCS#1) - Python SDK 专用 ===\"\ncat /tmp/tiger_rsa_pkcs1.pem\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== PUBLIC KEY ===\"\nopenssl rsa -in /tmp/tiger_rsa_pkcs1.pem -pubout 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":3015,"output":454,"cacheRead":60544,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":64013,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779153467143}}
