{"type":"message","id":"1259201e","parentId":"f1fb542a","timestamp":"2026-05-19T01:20:11.631Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The key format issue is that the private key in the user's config has `\\n` as literal characters rather than actual newlines. When passed to the Python SDK, the `\\n` characters are counted as part of the base64 string, making it invalid. But when the actual newlines are used, the base64 is valid (1624 chars, divisible by 4).\n\nThe user's code is a Coze Skill (JavaScript), not Python. The JavaScript code handles `\\n` replacement. So the config is fine for Coze. Let me just confirm the config is saved and report the sandbox network limitation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_44ac3affeb37498e97d562a8","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"rm -rf /tmp/tiger-test /tmp/tiger_test*.py /tmp/key_*.pem /tmp/tiger_*.pem","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":1656,"output":319,"cacheRead":75584,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":77559,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779153598560}}
