{"type":"message","id":"37f195bd","parentId":"e8497cd8","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:10:27.888Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the key information about Tiger's data permissions. Let me also check the fee structure and preparation page. But actually, the permission page already gives us a lot of useful information. Let me summarize the key findings for VAN.\n\nKey findings:\n1. Market data permissions are tied to account tier (assets/trading volume)\n2. There are different levels of market data (L1 basic, L2 depth)\n3. Historical data quotas are tied to account tier\n4. Hong Kong market data seems to be available (we already confirmed this works)\n5. US market data (Nasdaq Basic, etc.) requires specific permissions that may need to be purchased\n6. Free refresh mode only gives real-time quotes without order book/tick data\npaid subscription gives full real-time data with order book and tick data\n\nLet me also check what's in the fee page for completeness.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":29069,"output":402,"cacheRead":53248,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":82719,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779160219314}}
