200;padding-bottom:8px}/*! BEGIN HUB_CUSTOM_STYLES *//*! END HUB_CUSTOM_STYLES */\nvar storedColorMode = `system` === 'system' ? window.localStorage.getItem('color-scheme') : `system`\ndocument.querySelector('[data-color-mode]').setAttribute('data-color-mode', storedColorMode)\nUser and Account Types\nOrder and Trading Rules\nTrading and Data Fees\nData Permissions and Limitations\nCommand Line Interface (CLI)\nBasic Functionality Examples\nComplete Usage Example\nWarrants and Callable Bull/Bear Certificates\nCancel or Modify Orders\nGet Order Information\nQuery Account Information\nAccount Change Push Notifications\nAppendix 2: Enumeration Parameter Reference Table\nBasic Function Examples\nCancel or Modify Order\nEnvironment Requirements\nOperating System Requirements:\nProgramming Language Version Requirements: Python 3.8 and above\nWe recommend installing Python 3.8 or above. You can check the version by entering\nPython official download page\n, select the installation package for your operating system, and follow the prompts to complete the installation.\nInstalling Tiger Open API Python SDK\nis currently the fastest Python package manager, automatically creating virtual environments and managing dependencies:\nuv add tigeropen --upgrade\nAI Programming Tools (Recommended)\nAI programming tools can automatically read Tiger OpenAPI documentation. You can describe your needs in natural language to generate runnable SDK code, greatly lowering the barrier to entry.\nCreate a project environment and install\nusing any of the methods above\nPlace the configuration file\ntiger_openapi_config.properties\nin the project directory\nTiger OpenAPI Documentation\nas context for the AI tool (refer to each tool's instructions below)\nDescribe your needs in natural language, and the AI will read the documentation and generate the corresponding SDK code\nFor example, you can simply say: \"Get AAPL's daily K-line data for the last 30 days\" or \"Place a limit buy order for NVDA\", and the AI will automatically generate the complete code based on the documentation.\nCursor / Trae / Windsurf\nAdd documentation as context in your project:\n: Add the Tiger OpenAPI documentation URL in Settings > Docs, and the AI will automatically search it during conversations\n: Add documentation links or key pages to the Knowledge Base, and the AI will generate code based on the documentation\n: Reference online documentation via\n, or place documentation content in the project directory for the AI to read\nVS Code + GitHub Copilot\nextension in VS Code, and use the Chat panel to interact with AI to generate code. You can use\nto reference documentation or code files in the project as context.\nTerminal AI tools that can directly reference documentation links in conversations, and the AI will fetch and understand the documentation content:\n# Install Claude Code\nnpm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code\n\n# Start in the project directory\ncd my-tiger-project\nclaude\nAfter starting, send the documentation link to the AI, for example: \"Refer to\nhttps://quant.itigerup.com/openapi/py/overview/introduction\nand help me get position information\".\nFor Retail Users, Register through Personal Center\nBefore using the API, please first activate permissions. Individual users should visit the API official website to\nregister developer identity"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":2271,"aggregated":":root{--project-color-primary:#ffe200;--project-color-inverse:#222;--recipe-button-color:#00a1ff;--recipe-button-color-hover:#006199;--recipe-button-color-active:#004066;--recipe-button-color-focus:rgba(0, 161, 255, 0.25);--recipe-button-color-disabled:#ccecff}[id=enterprise] .ReadMeUI[is=AlgoliaSearch]{--project-color-primary:#ffe200;--project-color-inverse:#222}a{color:var(--color-link-primary,#00a1ff)}a:hover{color:var(--color-link-primary-darken-5,#006199)}a.text-muted:hover{color:var(--color-link-primary,#00a1ff)}.btn.btn-primary{backgrou