{"type":"message","id":"89b84d7f","parentId":"f23d8082","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:26:08.579Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me try a different approach - use JavaScript to extract just the article content.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_bf9d9a326ccf4c7ebeb1eee3","name":"browser","arguments":{"action":"act","targetId":"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33","kind":"evaluate","fn":"() => { const article = document.querySelector('article'); if (article) { const headings = article.querySelectorAll('h1, h2, h3'); const paragraphs = article.querySelectorAll('p, li, code, pre'); let text = []; headings.forEach(h => text.push('## ' + h.textContent.trim())); paragraphs.forEach(p => { const t = p.textContent.trim(); if (t.length > 5) text.push(t); }); return text.join('\\n').substring(0, 8000); } return 'No article found'; }"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":204,"output":219,"cacheRead":60928,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":61351,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779161163770}}
{"type":"message","id":"46c234f9","parentId":"89b84d7f","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:26:08.630Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_bf9d9a326ccf4c7ebeb1eee3","toolName":"browser","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"targetId\": \"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33\",\n  \"url\": \"https://docs-en.itigerup.com/docs/mcp\",\n  \"result\": \"## MCP Server\\n## Install [uv]\\n## Add MCP Server\\nYou can use our MCP tools built on the SDK for Tiger OpenAPI on any platform that supports MCP.\\nIf you haven't opened Tiger OpenAPI yet, please read Preparation to complete the permission application and obtain necessary information such as tiger id, private key, etc.\\nQuote permissions: Real-time market data queries (quotes, ticks, depth, etc.) require a separate API quote subscription, independent from in-app quote permissions. Historical data such as K-lines is available based on your subscription tier. See Quote Permissions for details.\\nIf you are using macOS/Linux systems, open \\\"Terminal\\\" and run the following command to complete the installation:\\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\\nNote: [uv] is a Python package and environment management tool, used here to run MCP Server.\\nFind the MCP entry in the tool you are using, select Manual Configuration, and paste the following content.\\nPlease replace your tiger id, your private key, and your account id with your actual values; also, if you want the server to run in read-only mode (disable trading operations), set TIGERMCP_READONLY to true, otherwise set to false.\\nTIGERMCP_READONLY\\n{\\n  \\\"mcpServers\\\": {\\n    \\\"tigermcp\\\": {\\n      \\\"command\\\": \\\"uvx\\\",\\n      \\\"args\\\": [\\n        \\\"--python\\\",\\n        \\\"3.13\\\",\\n        \\\"tigermcp\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"env\\\": {\\n        \\\"TIGEROPEN_TIGER_ID\\\": \\\"your tiger id\\\",\\n        \\\"TIGEROPEN_PRIVATE_KEY\\\": \\\"your private key\\\",\\n        \\\"TIGEROPEN_ACCOUNT\\\": \\\"your account id\\\",\\n        \\\"TIGERMCP_READONLY\\\": true\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n{\\n  \\\"mcpServers\\\": {\\n    \\\"tigermcp\\\": {\\n      \\\"command\\\": \\\"uvx\\\",\\n      \\\"args\\\": [\\n        \\\"--python\\\",\\n        \\\"3.13\\\",\\n        \\\"tigermcp\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"env\\\": {\\n        \\\"TIGEROPEN_TIGER_ID\\\": \\\"your tiger id\\\",\\n        \\\"TIGEROPEN_PRIVATE_KEY\\\": \\\"your private key\\\",\\n        \\\"TIGEROPEN_ACCOUNT\\\": \\\"your account id\\\",\\n        \\\"TIGERMCP_READONLY\\\": true\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\nIf the system is macOS 12 or earlier, you may encounter the following error when running mcp server:\\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: realpath: command not found\\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: /Users/tiger/python: No such file or directory\\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: exec: /Users/tiger/python: cannot execute: No such file or directory\\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: realpath: command not found\\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: /Users/tiger/python: No such file or directory\\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: exec: /Users/tiger/python: cannot execute: No such file or directory\\nThis is due to the missing realpath command, which needs to be installed.\\nFirst, open the terminal and type brew -v to check if the brew command exists. If an error occurs indicating the command doesn't exist, you need to install it first:\\nrealpath\\nbrew -v\\n/bin/bash -c \\\"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\\\"\\n/bin/bash -c \\\"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\\\"\\nThen, use brew to install coreutils:\\ncoreutils\\nbrew install coreutils\\nbrew install coreutils\\nAfter installation, you can try running the mcp server again.\\nDisclaimer\\nUpdated 20 days ago\\nInstall [uv]\\nAdd MCP Server\\nInstall [uv]\\nAdd MCP Server\"\n}"}],"details":{"ok":true,"targetId":"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33","url":"https://docs-en.itigerup.com/docs/mcp","result":"## MCP Server\n## Install [uv]\n## Add MCP Server\nYou can use our MCP tools built on the SDK for Tiger OpenAPI on any platform that supports MCP.\nIf you haven't opened Tiger OpenAPI yet, please read Preparation to complete the permission application and obtain necessary information such as tiger id, private key, etc.\nQuote permissions: Real-time market data queries (quotes, ticks, depth, etc.) require a separate API quote subscription, independent from in-app quote permissions. Historical data such as K-lines is available based on your subscription tier. See Quote Permissions for details.\nIf you are using macOS/Linux systems, open \"Terminal\" and run the following command to complete the installation:\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\nNote: [uv] is a Python package and environment management tool, used here to run MCP Server.\nFind the MCP entry in the tool you are using, select Manual Configuration, and paste the following content.\nPlease replace your tiger id, your private key, and your account id with your actual values; also, if you want the server to run in read-only mode (disable trading operations), set TIGERMCP_READONLY to true, otherwise set to false.\nTIGERMCP_READONLY\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"tigermcp\": {\n      \"command\": \"uvx\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \"--python\",\n        \"3.13\",\n        \"tigermcp\"\n      ],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"TIGEROPEN_TIGER_ID\": \"your tiger id\",\n        \"TIGEROPEN_PRIVATE_KEY\": \"your private key\",\n        \"TIGEROPEN_ACCOUNT\": \"your account id\",\n        \"TIGERMCP_READONLY\": true\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"tigermcp\": {\n      \"command\": \"uvx\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \"--python\",\n        \"3.13\",\n        \"tigermcp\"\n      ],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"TIGEROPEN_TIGER_ID\": \"your tiger id\",\n        \"TIGEROPEN_PRIVATE_KEY\": \"your private key\",\n        \"TIGEROPEN_ACCOUNT\": \"your account id\",\n        \"TIGERMCP_READONLY\": true\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\nIf the system is macOS 12 or earlier, you may encounter the following error when running mcp server:\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: realpath: command not found\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: /Users/tiger/python: No such file or directory\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: exec: /Users/tiger/python: cannot execute: No such file or directory\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: realpath: command not found\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: /Users/tiger/python: No such file or directory\n/Users/tiger/.cache/uv/archive-v0/5iV7KVbKUQlypQW-eBHBn/bin/tigermcp: line 2: exec: /Users/tiger/python: cannot execute: No such file or directory\nThis is due to the missing realpath command, which needs to be installed.\nFirst, open the terminal and type brew -v to check if the brew command exists. If an error occurs indicating the command doesn't exist, you need to install it first:\nrealpath\nbrew -v\n/bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\"\n/bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\"\nThen, use brew to install coreutils:\ncoreutils\nbrew install coreutils\nbrew install coreutils\nAfter installation, you can try running the mcp server again.\nDisclaimer\nUpdated 20 days ago\nInstall [uv]\nAdd MCP Server\nInstall [uv]\nAdd MCP Server"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779161168627}}
