{"type":"message","id":"fecf0de3","parentId":"29f3ae40","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:26:13.743Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0dc22872fe5947a2a2580328","toolName":"browser","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"targetId\": \"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33\",\n  \"url\": \"https://docs-en.itigerup.com/docs/cli\"\n}"}],"details":{"ok":true,"targetId":"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33","url":"https://docs-en.itigerup.com/docs/cli"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779161173741}}
{"type":"message","id":"49915359","parentId":"fecf0de3","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:26:17.095Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me get the CLI documentation content.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_e567b2cd4cba4d8a8e8811e9","name":"browser","arguments":{"action":"act","targetId":"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33","kind":"evaluate","fn":"() => { const article = document.querySelector('article'); if (article) { const headings = article.querySelectorAll('h1, h2, h3'); const paragraphs = article.querySelectorAll('p, li, code, pre'); let text = []; headings.forEach(h => text.push('## ' + h.textContent.trim())); paragraphs.forEach(p => { const t = p.textContent.trim(); if (t.length > 5) text.push(t); }); return text.join('\\n').substring(0, 8000); } return 'No article found'; }"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":228,"output":203,"cacheRead":62400,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":62831,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779161173744}}
{"type":"message","id":"fe446ccd","parentId":"49915359","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:26:17.143Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e567b2cd4cba4d8a8e8811e9","toolName":"browser","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"targetId\": \"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33\",\n  \"url\": \"https://docs-en.itigerup.com/docs/cli\",\n  \"result\": \"## Command Line Interface (CLI)\\n## Installation\\n## Configuration\\n## Global Options\\n## Stock Quotes\\n## Stock Scanner\\n## Options Data\\n## Futures Data\\n## Capital Flow\\n## Fundamental Data\\n## Order Management\\n## Positions\\n## Transaction History\\n## Account Information\\n## Real-Time Streaming\\n## Configuration Management\\n## Other Commands\\n## Output Formats\\n## Rate Limits\\nThe Tiger OpenAPI Python SDK provides a tigeropen command-line tool that allows you to query market data, manage orders, view account information, and more directly from the terminal — no code required.\\ntigeropen\\nWe recommend using the one-line install script, which automatically detects and uses the best available method (uv > pipx > pip):\\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tigerfintech/openapi-python-sdk/master/install.sh | sh\\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tigerfintech/openapi-python-sdk/master/install.sh | sh\\nIf you prefer to install manually, we recommend uv (a fast Python package manager):\\n# Install uv (if not already installed)\\n# macOS / Linux:\\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\\n# Or via pip:\\npip install uv\\n\\n# Install tigeropen with uv\\nuv pip install tigeropen\\n# Install uv (if not already installed)\\n# macOS / Linux:\\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\\n# Or via pip:\\npip install uv\\n\\n# Install tigeropen with uv\\nuv pip install tigeropen\\nYou can also install via pipx or pip:\\n# pipx (creates an isolated environment automatically)\\npipx install tigeropen\\n\\n# pip (installs to current environment, suitable when you also need the SDK in your code)\\npip install tigeropen\\n# pipx (creates an isolated environment automatically)\\npipx install tigeropen\\n\\n# pip (installs to current environment, suitable when you also need the SDK in your code)\\npip install tigeropen\\nAfter installation, run tigeropen in your terminal to see the usage guide.\\ntigeropen\\nBefore using the CLI, you need to set up your Tiger OpenAPI credentials. There are two ways to configure:\\nRun the following command and follow the prompts to enter your Tiger ID, Account, Private Key, etc.:\\ntigeropen config init\\ntigeropen config init\\nConfiguration will be saved to the ~/.tigeropen/ directory.\\n~/.tigeropen/\\nThe following options can be used with any subcommand:\\n-f, --format\\n-c, --config-path\\n-l, --language\\n-v, --verbose\\n-h, --help\\nQuote permissions: Real-time market data (quotes, ticks, depth, etc.) requires a separate API quote subscription, independent from in-app quote permissions. Historical data such as K-lines is available based on your subscription tier. See Quote Permissions for details.\\n# Get real-time stock quotes\\ntigeropen quote briefs AAPL TSLA\\n\\n# Include pre/after market data\\ntigeropen quote briefs AAPL --hour-trading\\n\\n# Get daily K-line data (default: last 251 bars)\\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period day\\n\\n# Get 5-minute K-line with custom limit\\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period 5min --limit 50\\n\\n# Specify time range\\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period day --begin-time 2025-01-01 --end-time 2025-03-01\\n\\n# Get today's intraday data\\ntigeropen quote timeline AAPL\\n\\n# Get intraday data for a specific date\\ntigeropen quote timeline AAPL --date 2025-03-20\\n\\n# Tick-by-tick data\\ntigeropen quote ticks AAPL --limit 100\\n\\n# Order book (depth)\\ntigeropen quote depth AAPL --market US\\n\\n# Market status\\ntigeropen quote market-status --market US\\n\\n# Stock symbol list\\ntigeropen quote symbols --market US\\n# Get real-time stock quotes\\ntigeropen quote briefs AAPL TSLA\\n\\n# Include pre/after market data\\ntigeropen quote briefs AAPL --hour-trading\\n\\n# Get daily K-line data (default: last 251 bars)\\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period day\\n\\n# Get 5-minute K-line with custom limit\\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period 5min --limit 50\\n\\n# Specify time range\\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period day --begin-time 2025-01-01 --end-time 2025-03-01\\n\\n# Get today's intraday data\\ntigeropen quote timeline AAPL\\n\\n# Get intraday data for a specific date\\ntigeropen quote timeline AAPL --date 2025-03-20\\n\\n# Tick-by-tick data\\ntigeropen quote ticks AAPL --limit 100\\n\\n# Order book (depth)\\ntigeropen quote depth AAPL --market US\\n\\n# Market status\\ntigeropen quote market-status --market US\\n\\n# Stock symbol list\\ntigeropen quote symbols --market US\\n# Top gainers today (preset)\\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter gainers --sort acc.ChangeRate --sort-dir DESC\\n\\n# Large-cap US stocks with P/E under 20\\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter MarketValue:1e10: --filter PeTTM::20 --sort MarketValue\\n\\n# High annual ROE stocks\\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter acc.ROE:0.15::ANNUAL --sort acc.ROE:ANNUAL --sort-dir DESC\\n\\n# Stocks with options available\\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter tag.OptionsAvailable:1\\n\\n# HK market scan\\ntigeropen quote scanner --market HK --filter MarketValue:1e9: --sort MarketValue\\n# Top gainers today (preset)\\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter gainers --sort acc.ChangeRate --sort-dir DESC\\n\\n# Large-cap US stocks with P/E under 20\\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter MarketValue:1e10: --filter PeTTM::20 --sort MarketValue\\n\\n# High annual ROE stocks\\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter acc.ROE:0.15::ANNUAL --sort acc.ROE:ANNUAL --sort-dir DESC\\n\\n# Stocks with options available\\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter tag.OptionsAvailable:1\\n\\n# HK market scan\\ntigeropen quote scanner --market HK --filter MarketValue:1e9: --sort MarketValue\\n--filter format:\\n--filter\\nFIELD:min:max — numeric range, e.g. PeTTM::20 (P/E below 20), MarketValue:1e9: (market cap above 1B)\\nFIELD:min:max\\nPeTTM::20\\nMarketValue:1e9:\\nacc.FIELD:min:max:PERIOD — accumulate field, PERIOD: ANNUAL, QUARTERLY, SEMIANNUAL\\nacc.FIELD:min:max:PERIOD\\nANNUAL\\nQUARTERLY\\nSEMIANNUAL\\nfin.FIELD:min:max — financial field (LTM)\\nfin.FIELD:min:max\\ntag.FIELD:tag1,tag2 — tag filter, e.g. tag.OptionsAvailable:1\\ntag.FIELD:tag1,tag2\\ntag.OptionsAvailable:1\\nPresets: gainers (intraday change > 5%), losers (intraday change < -5%)\\ngainers\\nlosers\\n# Get option expiration dates\\ntigeropen quote option expirations AAPL\\n\\n# Get option chain\\ntigeropen quote option chain AAPL 2025-06-20\\n\\n# Get option quotes\\ntigeropen quote option briefs \\\"AAPL  250620C00200000\\\"\\n\\n# Get option K-line data\\ntigeropen quote option bars \\\"AAPL  250620C00200000\\\" --period day\\n# Get option expiration dates\\ntigeropen quote option expirations AAPL\\n\\n# Get option chain\\ntigeropen quote option chain AAPL 2025-06-20\\n\\n# Get option quotes\\ntigeropen quote option briefs \\\"AAPL  250620C00200000\\\"\\n\\n# Get option K-line data\\ntigeropen quote option bars \\\"AAPL  250620C00200000\\\" --period day\\n# List available futures exchanges\\ntigeropen quote future exchanges\\n\\n# List futures contracts for an exchange\\ntigeropen quote future contracts CME\\n\\n# Get futures quotes\\ntigeropen quote future briefs CL2509\\n\\n# Get futures K-line data\\ntigeropen quote future bars CL2509 --period day\\n# List available futures exchanges\\ntigeropen quote future exchanges\\n\\n# List futures contracts for an exchange\\ntigeropen quote future contracts CME\\n\\n# Get futures quotes\\ntigeropen quote future briefs CL2509\\n\\n# Get futures K-line data\\ntigeropen quote future bars CL2509 --period day\\n# Get capital flow data\\ntigeropen quote capital flow AAPL --market US --period day\\n\\n# Get capital distribution\\ntigeropen quote capital distribution AAPL --market US\\n# Get capital flow data\\ntigeropen quote capital flow AAPL --market US --period day\\n\\n# Get capital distribution\\ntigeropen quote capital distribution AAPL --market US\\n# Get financial reports\\ntigeropen quote fundamental financial AAPL --fields total_revenue,net_income --period-type ANNUAL\\n\\n# Get dividend data\\ntigeropen quote fundamental dividend AAPL --begin-date 2024-01-01 --end-date 2025-01-01\\n\\n# Get earnings calendar\\ntigeropen quote fundamental earnings --begin-date 2025-03-01 --end-date 2025-03-31\\n# Get financial reports\\ntigeropen quote fundamental financial AAPL --fields total_revenue,net_income --period-type ANNUAL\\n\\n# Get dividend data\\ntigeropen quote fundamental dividend AAPL --begin-date 2024-01-01 --end-date 2025-01-01\\n\\n# Get earnings calendar\\ntigeropen quote fundamental earnings --begin-date 2\"\n}"}],"details":{"ok":true,"targetId":"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33","url":"https://docs-en.itigerup.com/docs/cli","result":"## Command Line Interface (CLI)\n## Installation\n## Configuration\n## Global Options\n## Stock Quotes\n## Stock Scanner\n## Options Data\n## Futures Data\n## Capital Flow\n## Fundamental Data\n## Order Management\n## Positions\n## Transaction History\n## Account Information\n## Real-Time Streaming\n## Configuration Management\n## Other Commands\n## Output Formats\n## Rate Limits\nThe Tiger OpenAPI Python SDK provides a tigeropen command-line tool that allows you to query market data, manage orders, view account information, and more directly from the terminal — no code required.\ntigeropen\nWe recommend using the one-line install script, which automatically detects and uses the best available method (uv > pipx > pip):\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tigerfintech/openapi-python-sdk/master/install.sh | sh\ncurl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tigerfintech/openapi-python-sdk/master/install.sh | sh\nIf you prefer to install manually, we recommend uv (a fast Python package manager):\n# Install uv (if not already installed)\n# macOS / Linux:\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\n# Or via pip:\npip install uv\n\n# Install tigeropen with uv\nuv pip install tigeropen\n# Install uv (if not already installed)\n# macOS / Linux:\ncurl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh\n# Or via pip:\npip install uv\n\n# Install tigeropen with uv\nuv pip install tigeropen\nYou can also install via pipx or pip:\n# pipx (creates an isolated environment automatically)\npipx install tigeropen\n\n# pip (installs to current environment, suitable when you also need the SDK in your code)\npip install tigeropen\n# pipx (creates an isolated environment automatically)\npipx install tigeropen\n\n# pip (installs to current environment, suitable when you also need the SDK in your code)\npip install tigeropen\nAfter installation, run tigeropen in your terminal to see the usage guide.\ntigeropen\nBefore using the CLI, you need to set up your Tiger OpenAPI credentials. There are two ways to configure:\nRun the following command and follow the prompts to enter your Tiger ID, Account, Private Key, etc.:\ntigeropen config init\ntigeropen config init\nConfiguration will be saved to the ~/.tigeropen/ directory.\n~/.tigeropen/\nThe following options can be used with any subcommand:\n-f, --format\n-c, --config-path\n-l, --language\n-v, --verbose\n-h, --help\nQuote permissions: Real-time market data (quotes, ticks, depth, etc.) requires a separate API quote subscription, independent from in-app quote permissions. Historical data such as K-lines is available based on your subscription tier. See Quote Permissions for details.\n# Get real-time stock quotes\ntigeropen quote briefs AAPL TSLA\n\n# Include pre/after market data\ntigeropen quote briefs AAPL --hour-trading\n\n# Get daily K-line data (default: last 251 bars)\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period day\n\n# Get 5-minute K-line with custom limit\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period 5min --limit 50\n\n# Specify time range\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period day --begin-time 2025-01-01 --end-time 2025-03-01\n\n# Get today's intraday data\ntigeropen quote timeline AAPL\n\n# Get intraday data for a specific date\ntigeropen quote timeline AAPL --date 2025-03-20\n\n# Tick-by-tick data\ntigeropen quote ticks AAPL --limit 100\n\n# Order book (depth)\ntigeropen quote depth AAPL --market US\n\n# Market status\ntigeropen quote market-status --market US\n\n# Stock symbol list\ntigeropen quote symbols --market US\n# Get real-time stock quotes\ntigeropen quote briefs AAPL TSLA\n\n# Include pre/after market data\ntigeropen quote briefs AAPL --hour-trading\n\n# Get daily K-line data (default: last 251 bars)\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period day\n\n# Get 5-minute K-line with custom limit\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period 5min --limit 50\n\n# Specify time range\ntigeropen quote bars AAPL --period day --begin-time 2025-01-01 --end-time 2025-03-01\n\n# Get today's intraday data\ntigeropen quote timeline AAPL\n\n# Get intraday data for a specific date\ntigeropen quote timeline AAPL --date 2025-03-20\n\n# Tick-by-tick data\ntigeropen quote ticks AAPL --limit 100\n\n# Order book (depth)\ntigeropen quote depth AAPL --market US\n\n# Market status\ntigeropen quote market-status --market US\n\n# Stock symbol list\ntigeropen quote symbols --market US\n# Top gainers today (preset)\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter gainers --sort acc.ChangeRate --sort-dir DESC\n\n# Large-cap US stocks with P/E under 20\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter MarketValue:1e10: --filter PeTTM::20 --sort MarketValue\n\n# High annual ROE stocks\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter acc.ROE:0.15::ANNUAL --sort acc.ROE:ANNUAL --sort-dir DESC\n\n# Stocks with options available\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter tag.OptionsAvailable:1\n\n# HK market scan\ntigeropen quote scanner --market HK --filter MarketValue:1e9: --sort MarketValue\n# Top gainers today (preset)\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter gainers --sort acc.ChangeRate --sort-dir DESC\n\n# Large-cap US stocks with P/E under 20\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter MarketValue:1e10: --filter PeTTM::20 --sort MarketValue\n\n# High annual ROE stocks\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter acc.ROE:0.15::ANNUAL --sort acc.ROE:ANNUAL --sort-dir DESC\n\n# Stocks with options available\ntigeropen quote scanner --filter tag.OptionsAvailable:1\n\n# HK market scan\ntigeropen quote scanner --market HK --filter MarketValue:1e9: --sort MarketValue\n--filter format:\n--filter\nFIELD:min:max — numeric range, e.g. PeTTM::20 (P/E below 20), MarketValue:1e9: (market cap above 1B)\nFIELD:min:max\nPeTTM::20\nMarketValue:1e9:\nacc.FIELD:min:max:PERIOD — accumulate field, PERIOD: ANNUAL, QUARTERLY, SEMIANNUAL\nacc.FIELD:min:max:PERIOD\nANNUAL\nQUARTERLY\nSEMIANNUAL\nfin.FIELD:min:max — financial field (LTM)\nfin.FIELD:min:max\ntag.FIELD:tag1,tag2 — tag filter, e.g. tag.OptionsAvailable:1\ntag.FIELD:tag1,tag2\ntag.OptionsAvailable:1\nPresets: gainers (intraday change > 5%), losers (intraday change < -5%)\ngainers\nlosers\n# Get option expiration dates\ntigeropen quote option expirations AAPL\n\n# Get option chain\ntigeropen quote option chain AAPL 2025-06-20\n\n# Get option quotes\ntigeropen quote option briefs \"AAPL  250620C00200000\"\n\n# Get option K-line data\ntigeropen quote option bars \"AAPL  250620C00200000\" --period day\n# Get option expiration dates\ntigeropen quote option expirations AAPL\n\n# Get option chain\ntigeropen quote option chain AAPL 2025-06-20\n\n# Get option quotes\ntigeropen quote option briefs \"AAPL  250620C00200000\"\n\n# Get option K-line data\ntigeropen quote option bars \"AAPL  250620C00200000\" --period day\n# List available futures exchanges\ntigeropen quote future exchanges\n\n# List futures contracts for an exchange\ntigeropen quote future contracts CME\n\n# Get futures quotes\ntigeropen quote future briefs CL2509\n\n# Get futures K-line data\ntigeropen quote future bars CL2509 --period day\n# List available futures exchanges\ntigeropen quote future exchanges\n\n# List futures contracts for an exchange\ntigeropen quote future contracts CME\n\n# Get futures quotes\ntigeropen quote future briefs CL2509\n\n# Get futures K-line data\ntigeropen quote future bars CL2509 --period day\n# Get capital flow data\ntigeropen quote capital flow AAPL --market US --period day\n\n# Get capital distribution\ntigeropen quote capital distribution AAPL --market US\n# Get capital flow data\ntigeropen quote capital flow AAPL --market US --period day\n\n# Get capital distribution\ntigeropen quote capital distribution AAPL --market US\n# Get financial reports\ntigeropen quote fundamental financial AAPL --fields total_revenue,net_income --period-type ANNUAL\n\n# Get dividend data\ntigeropen quote fundamental dividend AAPL --begin-date 2024-01-01 --end-date 2025-01-01\n\n# Get earnings calendar\ntigeropen quote fundamental earnings --begin-date 2025-03-01 --end-date 2025-03-31\n# Get financial reports\ntigeropen quote fundamental financial AAPL --fields total_revenue,net_income --period-type ANNUAL\n\n# Get dividend data\ntigeropen quote fundamental dividend AAPL --begin-date 2024-01-01 --end-date 2025-01-01\n\n# Get earnings calendar\ntigeropen quote fundamental earnings --begin-date 2"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779161177141}}
