{"type":"message","id":"2a8abe13","parentId":"b77e7ff1","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:26:22.344Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c85d74753f654b1195781cc6","toolName":"browser","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"targetId\": \"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33\",\n  \"url\": \"https://docs-en.itigerup.com/docs/skill\"\n}"}],"details":{"ok":true,"targetId":"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33","url":"https://docs-en.itigerup.com/docs/skill"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779161182341}}
{"type":"message","id":"09b0274a","parentId":"2a8abe13","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:26:25.593Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me get the AI Skill Plugin documentation content.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_95f1ba41e83e46079084dad5","name":"browser","arguments":{"action":"act","targetId":"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33","kind":"evaluate","fn":"() => { const article = document.querySelector('article'); if (article) { const headings = article.querySelectorAll('h1, h2, h3'); const paragraphs = article.querySelectorAll('p, li, code, pre'); let text = []; headings.forEach(h => text.push('## ' + h.textContent.trim())); paragraphs.forEach(p => { const t = p.textContent.trim(); if (t.length > 5) text.push(t); }); return text.join('\\n').substring(0, 6000); } return 'No article found'; }"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"xiaomimimo","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","usage":{"input":181,"output":207,"cacheRead":65216,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":65604,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779161182345}}
{"type":"message","id":"087b25cf","parentId":"09b0274a","timestamp":"2026-05-19T03:26:25.640Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_95f1ba41e83e46079084dad5","toolName":"browser","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"targetId\": \"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33\",\n  \"url\": \"https://docs-en.itigerup.com/docs/skill\",\n  \"result\": \"## AI Skill Plugin\\n## Installation\\n## Prerequisites\\n## Skill Modules\\n## Usage Examples\\n## How It Works\\n## Supported AI Tools\\n## Repository\\nTiger OpenAPI provides an AI Skill plugin that follows the Agent Skills open standard, supporting 40+ AI coding tools including Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini CLI, GitHub Copilot, VS Code, OpenAI Codex, and more.\\nOnce installed, AI tools can help you query market data, place orders, manage accounts, and more through natural language — no need to manually look up API documentation.\\nInstall with a single command using npx skills:\\nnpx skills\\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill\\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill\\nThe CLI auto-detects your installed AI coding tools and guides you through scope selection (project / global).\\nMore installation options:\\n# List available skills\\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill --list\\n\\n# Install for a specific tool\\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill -a claude-code\\n\\n# Install globally (available across all projects)\\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill -g\\n\\n# Install to all detected tools\\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill --all\\n# List available skills\\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill --list\\n\\n# Install for a specific tool\\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill -a claude-code\\n\\n# Install globally (available across all projects)\\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill -g\\n\\n# Install to all detected tools\\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill --all\\nYou can also install via ClawHub:\\nnpx clawhub install tigerbrokers\\nnpx clawhub install tigerbrokers\\ngit clone https://github.com/tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill.git ~/tigeropen-skill\\nclaude --plugin-dir ~/tigeropen-skill\\ngit clone https://github.com/tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill.git ~/tigeropen-skill\\nclaude --plugin-dir ~/tigeropen-skill\\nClone the repository first, then copy the skill directory for your SDK:\\ngit clone https://github.com/tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill.git /tmp/tigeropen-skill\\ngit clone https://github.com/tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill.git /tmp/tigeropen-skill\\nChoose the skill directory name for your language:\\ntigeropen\\ntigeropen-java\\ntigeropen-cpp\\ntigeropen-csharp\\ntigeropen-go\\ntigeropen-rust\\ntigeropen-typescript\\n# Global (all projects) — replace \\\"tigeropen\\\" with your SDK's directory name\\ncp -r /tmp/tigeropen-skill/skills/tigeropen ~/.claude/skills/\\nrm -rf /tmp/tigeropen-skill\\n\\n# Project-specific\\nmkdir -p .claude/skills\\ncp -r /tmp/tigeropen-skill/skills/tigeropen .claude/skills/\\n# Global (all projects) — replace \\\"tigeropen\\\" with your SDK's directory name\\ncp -r /tmp/tigeropen-skill/skills/tigeropen ~/.claude/skills/\\nrm -rf /tmp/tigeropen-skill\\n\\n# Project-specific\\nmkdir -p .claude/skills\\ncp -r /tmp/tigeropen-skill/skills/tigeropen .claude/skills/\\nInstall the Python SDK: pip install tigeropen\\npip install tigeropen\\nHave a Tiger Brokers account with API access (Developer Page)\\nHave your tiger_id, private key file, and account ready\\ntiger_id\\naccount\\nThe skill includes the following modules. The AI will automatically load the relevant reference based on your request:\\nAfter installing, simply use natural language in your AI tool:\\n> Get real-time quotes for AAPL and TSLA\\n\\n> Buy 100 shares of AAPL with a limit order at $150\\n\\n> Fetch AAPL daily K-line data for the last 30 days and plot it\\n\\n> Show my account assets and current positions\\n\\n> Get AAPL option chain expiring next month, filter delta 0.3-0.7\\n\\n> Subscribe to real-time quote updates for AAPL and TSLA\\n> Get real-time quotes for AAPL and TSLA\\n\\n> Buy 100 shares of AAPL with a limit order at $150\\n\\n> Fetch AAPL daily K-line data for the last 30 days and plot it\\n\\n> Show my account assets and current positions\\n\\n> Get AAPL option chain expiring next month, filter delta 0.3-0.7\\n\\n> Subscribe to real-time quote updates for AAPL and TSLA\\nAn AI Skill is essentially a set of structured reference documents that teach AI coding tools how to correctly call Tiger OpenAPI. When you describe your needs in an AI tool:\\nThe AI identifies your intent (e.g., \\\"get quotes\\\", \\\"place order\\\")\\nAutomatically loads the relevant reference document (e.g., quote.md, trade.md)\\nGenerates correct code based on the API specifications and code examples in the document\\nExecutes the code and returns results\\nThis means you don't need to memorize API details — just describe what you want to do in natural language.\\nThe skill follows the Agent Skills open standard and supports the following AI coding tools (partial list):\\nClaude Code — Anthropic's official CLI\\nCursor — AI code editor\\nGemini CLI — Google Gemini command-line tool\\nGitHub Copilot — GitHub AI programming assistant\\nVS Code — Supported via extensions\\nOpenAI Codex — OpenAI coding tool\\nKiro — AWS AI IDE\\nTrae — ByteDance AI IDE\\nPlus 40+ other tools supporting the Agent Skills standard.\\nGitHub: tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill\\nDisclaimer\\nUpdated 25 days ago\\nInstallation\\nPrerequisites\\nSkill Modules\\nUsage Examples\\nHow It Works\\nSupported AI Tools\\nRepository\\nInstallation\\nPrerequisites\\nSkill Modules\\nUsage Examples\\nHow It Works\\nSupported AI Tools\\nRepository\"\n}"}],"details":{"ok":true,"targetId":"DF674514C99A043BFD3BEF081A048A33","url":"https://docs-en.itigerup.com/docs/skill","result":"## AI Skill Plugin\n## Installation\n## Prerequisites\n## Skill Modules\n## Usage Examples\n## How It Works\n## Supported AI Tools\n## Repository\nTiger OpenAPI provides an AI Skill plugin that follows the Agent Skills open standard, supporting 40+ AI coding tools including Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini CLI, GitHub Copilot, VS Code, OpenAI Codex, and more.\nOnce installed, AI tools can help you query market data, place orders, manage accounts, and more through natural language — no need to manually look up API documentation.\nInstall with a single command using npx skills:\nnpx skills\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill\nThe CLI auto-detects your installed AI coding tools and guides you through scope selection (project / global).\nMore installation options:\n# List available skills\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill --list\n\n# Install for a specific tool\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill -a claude-code\n\n# Install globally (available across all projects)\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill -g\n\n# Install to all detected tools\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill --all\n# List available skills\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill --list\n\n# Install for a specific tool\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill -a claude-code\n\n# Install globally (available across all projects)\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill -g\n\n# Install to all detected tools\nnpx skills add tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill --all\nYou can also install via ClawHub:\nnpx clawhub install tigerbrokers\nnpx clawhub install tigerbrokers\ngit clone https://github.com/tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill.git ~/tigeropen-skill\nclaude --plugin-dir ~/tigeropen-skill\ngit clone https://github.com/tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill.git ~/tigeropen-skill\nclaude --plugin-dir ~/tigeropen-skill\nClone the repository first, then copy the skill directory for your SDK:\ngit clone https://github.com/tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill.git /tmp/tigeropen-skill\ngit clone https://github.com/tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill.git /tmp/tigeropen-skill\nChoose the skill directory name for your language:\ntigeropen\ntigeropen-java\ntigeropen-cpp\ntigeropen-csharp\ntigeropen-go\ntigeropen-rust\ntigeropen-typescript\n# Global (all projects) — replace \"tigeropen\" with your SDK's directory name\ncp -r /tmp/tigeropen-skill/skills/tigeropen ~/.claude/skills/\nrm -rf /tmp/tigeropen-skill\n\n# Project-specific\nmkdir -p .claude/skills\ncp -r /tmp/tigeropen-skill/skills/tigeropen .claude/skills/\n# Global (all projects) — replace \"tigeropen\" with your SDK's directory name\ncp -r /tmp/tigeropen-skill/skills/tigeropen ~/.claude/skills/\nrm -rf /tmp/tigeropen-skill\n\n# Project-specific\nmkdir -p .claude/skills\ncp -r /tmp/tigeropen-skill/skills/tigeropen .claude/skills/\nInstall the Python SDK: pip install tigeropen\npip install tigeropen\nHave a Tiger Brokers account with API access (Developer Page)\nHave your tiger_id, private key file, and account ready\ntiger_id\naccount\nThe skill includes the following modules. The AI will automatically load the relevant reference based on your request:\nAfter installing, simply use natural language in your AI tool:\n> Get real-time quotes for AAPL and TSLA\n\n> Buy 100 shares of AAPL with a limit order at $150\n\n> Fetch AAPL daily K-line data for the last 30 days and plot it\n\n> Show my account assets and current positions\n\n> Get AAPL option chain expiring next month, filter delta 0.3-0.7\n\n> Subscribe to real-time quote updates for AAPL and TSLA\n> Get real-time quotes for AAPL and TSLA\n\n> Buy 100 shares of AAPL with a limit order at $150\n\n> Fetch AAPL daily K-line data for the last 30 days and plot it\n\n> Show my account assets and current positions\n\n> Get AAPL option chain expiring next month, filter delta 0.3-0.7\n\n> Subscribe to real-time quote updates for AAPL and TSLA\nAn AI Skill is essentially a set of structured reference documents that teach AI coding tools how to correctly call Tiger OpenAPI. When you describe your needs in an AI tool:\nThe AI identifies your intent (e.g., \"get quotes\", \"place order\")\nAutomatically loads the relevant reference document (e.g., quote.md, trade.md)\nGenerates correct code based on the API specifications and code examples in the document\nExecutes the code and returns results\nThis means you don't need to memorize API details — just describe what you want to do in natural language.\nThe skill follows the Agent Skills open standard and supports the following AI coding tools (partial list):\nClaude Code — Anthropic's official CLI\nCursor — AI code editor\nGemini CLI — Google Gemini command-line tool\nGitHub Copilot — GitHub AI programming assistant\nVS Code — Supported via extensions\nOpenAI Codex — OpenAI coding tool\nKiro — AWS AI IDE\nTrae — ByteDance AI IDE\nPlus 40+ other tools supporting the Agent Skills standard.\nGitHub: tigerfintech/tigeropen-skill\nDisclaimer\nUpdated 25 days ago\nInstallation\nPrerequisites\nSkill Modules\nUsage Examples\nHow It Works\nSupported AI Tools\nRepository\nInstallation\nPrerequisites\nSkill Modules\nUsage Examples\nHow It Works\nSupported AI Tools\nRepository"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779161185638}}
